WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.601 line:92%
-I have a few more questions

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:05.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
about your work in
the boy-band/girl-band genre

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:06.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
But when you first came
to New York,

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:08.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
where did you come
straight from?

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:10.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
Were you working in Florid
at the time?

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:12.212 line:92%
-I came from Universal Studios

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:13.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had worked at Disney
performing,

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:16.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then I was performing
at Universal Studios

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:20.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
at the "Murder, She Wrote"
post-production show.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:21.521 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Wow.

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:24.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I played an editor
or an ADR person

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
and different people
that put together

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:30.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
the episode of
"Murder, She Wrote."

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:34.667 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, so, I did that
and got a call

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.736 line:92%
to come to interview at "SNL

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:40.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
from the green room of
Universal Studios Theme Park

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:42.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm always fascinated
with people's first

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:44.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
New York City apartments.
What was your --

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:47.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
What did you find for yourself
as a young writer?

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:49.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I kind of took
the first one I saw

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:50.884 line:92%
'cause I thought it was cute

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:56.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
but the guy who was my
real-estate guy was sweating

00:00:56.089 --> 00:00:59.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was winter, I think.
It was late fall.

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:01.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he was sweating,
and he was super intense,

00:01:01.795 --> 00:01:04.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he kept using
the word "sick" as positive,

00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:05.632 size:78% position:39% line:92%
which I did not know.

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:07.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was not savvy
to the word "sick."

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:09.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
So he would just
show me things and go,

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:11.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The kitchen at this place
is sick!"

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:13.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I thought it was bad,
and I was like,

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:15.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Why is he so excited
about showing me

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:15.909 size:84% position:42% line:92%
this terrible kitchen?"

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:18.978
And then he described
this apartment, which, you know,

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:23.650
was soon after I realized
that all of real-estate

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
New York descriptions
are bull crap.

00:01:25.852 --> 00:01:30.657
And, so, he would say, you know,
"It has a prewar kitchen.

00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:34.294 size:84% position:42%
Vintage prewar kitchen
with copper detailing."

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:37.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I would picture this,
like, you know, weird tiling

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:40.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
that was all from the 1800
of copper.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:43.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was like
a '90s gay man's kitchen

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:44.170 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
that was teal,

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:47.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it had copper,
like, smears of paint

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:49.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
that looked like
a total '80s video.

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:52.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, then, it would say, like,
"garden window."

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:55.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you would look out,
and there was like, you know

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:56.216 line:92%
half a diaper and a pigeon

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:59.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then, like, one plant
that was half-dead.

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:01.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
So that was my first place
I lived.

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:05.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was next to H&amp;H Bagels,
which really was --

00:02:05.692 --> 00:02:09.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like Pepé Le Pew
going out every day

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:11.998 line:92%
to the smell of hot bread.

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:13.166 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And I still am.

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:17.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You wrote a sketch
called "7 Degrees Celsius.

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:18.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.
-This was a boy band.

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:20.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is cast members.
That's James Van Der Beek.

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:22.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That was "The Beek."
-"The Beek."

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:26.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you also got to write
for 'NSYNC.

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:29.449
-Yeah, you know, I did tha
as recurring characters,

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:30.150 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
those four --

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:34.220
You know, Parnell, Jimmy Fallon,
Horatio, and Kattan.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:36.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
They were --
I made a fake boy band.

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:38.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
They had really weird
facial hair,

00:02:38.525 --> 00:02:39.425 size:88% position:44% line:92%
and Will was the manager

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:43.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
and could only be 300 feet
from them due to a court case.

00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:47.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they had tinted glasses,
the whole shebang.

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:50.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I would write the song
and everything.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then 'NSYNC
was the music guest,

00:02:52.272 --> 00:02:54.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I think someone suggeste
or I suggested, like,

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:58.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
they can be the guest boy band
fake boy band on there.

00:02:58.845 --> 00:03:02.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I wrote the song
called "Hold the Pickle,"

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:04.217 line:92%
where they were fast-food guys

00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:06.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they had
McDonald's outfits on.

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:07.353 line:92%
And they were saying like...

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:09.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
♪♪ Hold the pickle
and do it up big ♪♪

00:03:09.789 --> 00:03:10.957 size:75% position:38% line:92%
And it was all about

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:13.459
being in love and holding
the pickle and all of this

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:14.894 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and it was very sexual.

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:17.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they couldn't
come and rehearse it

00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:18.498 line:92%
until the very last minute

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:21.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
And these guys took a whil
to learn things.

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:22.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
Wait. Wait. This crew?

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:25.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're telling me they weren't
great with choreography?

00:03:25.038 --> 00:03:25.772 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-It was a little rough.

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:27.874
It was like teaching goats how
to sing and dance at that point.

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:31.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
Jimmy and Parnell were --
They were all trying very hard

00:03:31.678 --> 00:03:33.713
But sometimes
they'd kind of be scattered off,

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:35.682 size:75% position:38%
and I'd have to keep
getting them back.

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:40.453
But 'NSYNC comes in,
and I hand them the, you know --

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:42.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
I say "Xeroxed"
because I'm 96 years old.

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:47.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I handed them, you know,
the copies of the thing.

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:48.394 line:92%
And they immediately, like

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:49.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
whispered to each other
in a huddle.

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:53.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then they get out
and do full four-part harmony,

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:56.970 size:88% position:44%
just kick flips, like,
full dance number to it.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:58.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, "Yeah,
let's just do this."

00:03:58.004 --> 00:04:01.674
And they do the whole thing.
And I was just in complete awe

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:03.076 line:92%
But that was really my exposur

00:04:03.076 --> 00:04:05.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the sort of
boy-group/girl-group stuff

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:09.482 size:84% position:42%
a lot, was when I was
sort of parodying them.

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:14.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have such a vivid memory
of coming home --

00:04:14.487 --> 00:04:16.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
on Sundays after "SNL,"

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:19.259 size:84% position:42%
it's like you're really
unpacking your feelings

00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:20.960 size:78% position:39% line:92%
of failure or success

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:23.730 size:78% position:39%
and your two martinis
at the after-party.

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:26.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I would just never leave
the apartment --

00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:30.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
that apartment with the sick -
the sick kitchen.

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:31.804 size:78% position:39%
I would never leave.
I would just order --

00:04:31.804 --> 00:04:34.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd wake up at 2:00,
order carryout,

00:04:34.474 --> 00:04:37.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
and just stay in that cocoon
all day.

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:40.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I turned on "TRL,"
at the time that was still on,

00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:43.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there were
all these screaming girls

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:44.117 size:78% position:39% line:92%
'cause it was 'NSYNC.

00:04:44.117 --> 00:04:48.354
And I looked down --
They showed down out the window.

00:04:48.354 --> 00:04:50.056 line:92%
And it was all these girls

00:04:50.056 --> 00:04:52.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was hours
after the show ended at "SNL."

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:55.028
And they had a giant banne
that said, "Hold the pickle.

00:04:55.028 --> 00:04:58.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
So that means all those
little girls sat and painted -

00:04:58.665 --> 00:05:00.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
poster paint
in the middle of the night -

00:05:00.366 --> 00:05:04.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
and made their mom go get
poster paint at Duane Reade.

00:05:04.237 --> 00:05:06.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they made this -- And
it was one of those first time

00:05:06.406 --> 00:05:09.075
at that show that I realized
how immediate everything was

00:05:09.075 --> 00:05:13.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
where it was like,
"Oh, this is really truly...

00:05:13.079 --> 00:05:15.848 size:75% position:38% line:92%
uh, live." [ Sighs ]

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:18.618 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Well, Paula, thank you.

00:05:18.618 --> 00:05:22.088
-I realized I had no real
big-bang finisher for that

00:05:22.088 --> 00:05:27.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I just thought I would
connect with you as an audienc

00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:29.062 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and just be human.

00:05:29.062 --> 00:05:31.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd be human
and connect with you.

00:05:31.431 --> 00:05:35.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Girls5eva" is streaming no
on Peacock.

